course: dictionary
lesson: 9654
title: Submersible: built to work underwater
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A submersible is a small vehicle that goes under the water. Scientists and explorers use submersibles to look at the deep sea and the ocean floor. Some carry one to three people, and others are steered by remote control from a ship or the land. «The Challenger Deep in the Mariana Trench is the deepest point of the ocean, nearly eleven kilometres down, and two men first reached it in 1960 in the submersible Trieste.» The bracket tells you what the word means, so you can use it there.
explain: Look at the word parts. Sub means under, as in submarine, and the rest of the word tells you the thing can go under the water and work there. Submersible can also be an adjective, which describes a thing. A submersible pump is a pump that works underwater, and a submersible watch can be used in water.
explain: Do not mix up a submersible and a submarine. A submarine is bigger and can travel on its own for long trips. A submersible is usually smaller and is used for exploring, such as looking at shipwrecks like the Titanic. Use the context to decide which one the writer means.
fact: A submersible is a small underwater vehicle.
fact: Submersibles explore the deep sea, the ocean floor and shipwrecks.
fact: Some submersibles carry a crew of one to three people, and others are controlled by remote control.
fact: As an adjective, submersible means able to work or be used underwater, like a submersible pump.
fact: A submersible is different from a submarine, which is bigger and travels on its own for long trips.
exercise: «The Challenger Deep ... in the submersible Trieste.» What is a submersible? | A large aeroplane that flies over the sea | *A small underwater vehicle used to explore the deep sea | A kind of fish found near the surface | A tall tower on a ship
exercise: «...in the submersible (a small deep-diving craft) Trieste.» What does the bracket tell you about Trieste? | It is a fish | *It is a small craft that dives deep | It is a type of rock | It is a giant ship that never sinks
exercise: «A submersible pump keeps the water moving.» What does submersible mean here? | Very noisy | Made of wood | Able to fly high | *Able to work underwater
test: Which is usually bigger and travels on its own on long trips? | A diver's mask | A submersible | *A submarine | A pump
test: Which phrase uses submersible as an adjective? | *a submersible pump | two men in 1960 | a manned submersible | the Mariana Trench
exam: Which best describes a submersible? | A bird that dives for fish | A long tunnel under a river | *A small underwater vehicle that explores the deep sea | A large ship that carries thousands of passengers across the ocean
